md('# RAG security and red-team testing\n\nThis research measures actual local attacker objectives and legitimate task performance. The frozen quarantine policy fails on held-out tasks: its zero measured attacker success accompanies zero clean completion. It is a failed defense, not a security success. Deterministic authorization and integrity controls have separate fixture results. The public study is a reduced BIPIA adaptation plus original synthetic fixtures; no official benchmark score or general security guarantee is claimed.')
code("from pathlib import Path\nimport json, sys\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nROOT = Path.cwd()\nif ROOT.name == 'notebooks': ROOT = ROOT.parent\nassert (ROOT / 'reports/selection-freeze.json').exists()\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'src'))\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'scripts'))\nfrom figures import figure\ndef read(name): return json.loads((ROOT / 'reports' / name).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))\nmetrics = read('metrics.json')\nfreeze = read('selection-freeze.json')\nprint('Frozen selection:', freeze['selected_model'], freeze['selected_defense'])")
md('## Motivation and prior evidence\n\nEarlier projects found that citations did not prove support, verification could reject useful answers, and cache reuse depended on current permissions. Security evaluation must therefore preserve utility and measure the attack objective directly. OWASP LLM application guidance supplies risk categories, not certification. See `docs/provenance.md` for the benchmark papers, exact source links and attribution.')
code("environment = read('environment.json')\n{k: environment[k] for k in ['python','platform','physical_cores','logical_cores','gpu','prior_tracked_files']}")
md('## Threat model and protected assets\n\nLevels A through E cover one retrieved passage, one submitted document, one read-only tool response, a cache candidate and one synthetic tenant. System instructions, canonical permissions and the application registry remain trusted. There are no offensive requests to external services. The complete assumptions and residual risks are in `docs/threat-model.md`.')
code("from rag_security.policy import Document, Registry, Principal\nfrom rag_security.retrieval import retrieve\ndocs = [Document('public', 'The station uses amber.'), Document('private', 'SYNTHETIC_CANARY_DEMO', tenant='beta')]\nregistry = Registry(docs)\nprincipal = Principal('alpha', 'reader', frozenset({'public','private'}))\nassert [d.id for d in retrieve('station', docs, registry, principal)] == ['public']\nprint('Canonical permissions exclude the other tenant before ranking.')")
md('## Dataset provenance and partitions\n\nTableQA contexts and unchanged public attack strings come from pinned BIPIA files. Wikipedia-derived tables remain local under their upstream rights. Synthetic observatory development tasks and botanical evaluation tasks are reported separately. AgentDojo was researched but not executed. RAG-PIBench could not be acquired with verified dataset provenance and license, so it contributes no scores.')
