md('## Attack-family EDA\n\nOne fixed payload defines each public family. Repetition across tasks does not create new attack diversity. Public development and evaluation attack families are disjoint; only dialogue and encoded redirection support the corresponding synthetic transfer claim. Citation, poison and tool tests recur as diagnostics.')
code("fig = figure('families'); plt.show()")
md('## Clean RAG baseline\n\nBM25 ranks bounded local candidates. Both generators receive ordinary QA instructions and source identifiers. D0 retains normal authorization and a read-only dispatcher. Clean completion uses normalized exact match for public tables and a closed-color factual oracle for synthetic records. EM and token F1 remain separate diagnostics.')
